{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>That chews the cud, etc., and that parts the hoof, etc.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Torat Kohanim; Bekhorot 6a) that it comes to prohibit even [an animal that only partially] chews and parts [the hoof], if these are found in the belly of an unclean [animal]. And the plain sense of the verse follows this course: <b>מִמַּעֲלֵי הַגֵּרָה</b> ('that chews the cud') — this is the camel; <b>וּמִמַּפְרִיסֵי</b> etc. — this is the pig; that is, it says either this or this. Therefore one must note carefully that it says <b>וּמִמַּפְרִיסֵי</b> etc. [with the mem prefix], and it did not say <b>וּמַפְרִיסֵי</b>; understand this."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:55:13.811871728Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}